      "explanation": "Adjustment for measured factors cannot establish that every possible confounder has been eliminated. Unmeasured factors, imperfect measurement and incomplete adjustment can leave residual confounding. B is therefore the justified conclusion; a variable is not necessarily a confounder merely because it is a known disease risk factor.",
