    "stem": "In a longitudinal (cohort) study 100,000 women of more than 50 years of age were enrolled to observe the risk of chronic diseases over a period of next 10 years. First survey in the year 1950 showed that of the 100,000 women 10,000 women reported family history of rectal polyps. At the end of the study period (1960), 46 women had developed colon cancer; of which 11 were among those who had a family history of rectal polyps. What is the incidence of colon cancer in those without the family history of rectal polyps?",
